vambed-neo is a software test transcoder. It contains no DVSI code, no DVSI
firmware and no code derived from any DVSI product. It is provided for
testing reflectors and for education; audio quality is not a goal.

Components (fetched at the commits pinned in pins.env, not vendored here)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
- mbelib-neo, https://github.com/arancormonk/mbelib-neo
  GPL-2.0-or-later (project contributions; retained ISC mbelib notices and
  PFFFT license texts, see its LICENSE and LICENSES/). Used for AMBE+
  (3600x2400), AMBE+2 (3600x2450) and IMBE (4400) decoding and encoding.
- codec2, https://github.com/drowe67/codec2
  LGPL-2.1. Used for Codec2 3200 decoding and encoding.

Protocol
--------
The AMBEd wire protocol and its reply layouts follow the xlxd ambed
(GPL-3.0-or-later, LX3JL and contributors) and the protocol notes of
dv-testset. No source file of xlxd is copied into this repository.

DMR AMBE interleave
-------------------
The DMR AMBE dibit interleave tables in src/vn_codec.c (dmr_w, dmr_x, dmr_y,
dmr_z) are the rW, rX, rY, rZ tables of DSD (Digital Speech Decoder),
https://github.com/szechyjs/dsd, ISC licence:
